research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-2274-          "fact": "L5",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-2275-          "source": "lem-cauchy-complete-and-archimedean-imply-mct",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-2276-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json:2277:          "quote": "Let $F$ be an Archimedean ordered field ([[def-archimedean-field]]) with Cauchy\ncompleteness (CC). Then $F$ has the monotone convergence property (MCT) of\n[[def-completeness-properties]]: every nondecreasing sequence in $F$ that is\nbounded above converges in $F$.\n\nThe Archimedean hypothesis is not decoration. Without it the implication is\nfalse: $\\mathbb{R}((t^{-1}))$ has (CC) ([[thm-laurent-cauchy-complete]]) and\nfails (MCT), since (MCT) would force it to be Archimedean\n([[lem-mct-implies-archimedean]]) and it is not\n([[lem-laurent-non-archimedean]]).",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-2278-          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-2279-            "1.4"
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-2280-          ]
--
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-2283-          "fact": "L6",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-2284-          "source": "lem-mct-implies-archimedean",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-2285-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json:2286:          "quote": "Let $F$ be an ordered field with the monotone convergence property (MCT) of\n[[def-completeness-properties]]. Then $F$ is Archimedean\n([[def-archimedean-field]]).\n\nSo (MCT), like (BW) and like (LUB), carries the Archimedean property on its own,\nand the hypothesis attached to (CC) in\n[[lem-cauchy-complete-and-archimedean-imply-mct]] need not be attached here.\nThis is what lets [[rem-where-the-archimedean-hypothesis-is-needed]] sort the\nfive properties into those that do and those that do not.",

