research/audit/wave7-judge-adjudications.jsonl-12-{"id":"lem-completely-regular-topologies-come-from-continuous-pseudometrics","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"643397666453cb785c5e2d3a85d7bc1f94e7e53d4b2ab8164de8b36b34a6685e","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"82ff1c86a370fc25366dd85b92c5100dd2accd8e9325e273e78bcb732576120d","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T19:32:01Z","note":"Terra correctly catches the empty-image boundary wording: the source definition promises a function 'such that $f(x)=1$ and $f(y)=0$ for every $y\\in C$', not that an empty image equals a singleton. At $U=X$ the quantified zero condition is vacuous and the radius-$1/2$ conclusion remains immediate. This boundary gap closes in seconds and does not invalidate the theorem; the thirty-second rule makes it nonfatal and R1 forbids a wording edit."}
research/audit/wave7-judge-adjudications.jsonl-13-{"id":"lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"b1d4a52488c358a672f76204585edece88d67934217cd58953765c16e9f792cd","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"a8dc582edcf5b4d953fca347e65dfc74e6b0cc220385c526c38794d8cb656d85","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T19:32:01Z","note":"The cited lemma states verbatim '$-|x| \\le x \\le |x|$' and, for $c>0$, '$|x| < c \\iff -c < x < c$.' The non-strict equivalence follows by the same two definition cases, or directly from the first displayed chain plus $|u|=u$ or $-u$. This is an immediate closure and nonfatal under the binding threshold; no mutation is licensed."}
research/audit/wave7-judge-adjudications.jsonl:14:{"id":"def-completeness-properties","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"e914b9b8ade76107942c54b597bf1a03ea79b6b0ff32ef23d44c7a8cd36b286c","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"other","item_sha256":"4578fa8b9599dcfd41b9ba86585ad98711144a421c0b71c5f6187a33fd6d07b3","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T19:32:01Z","note":"Terra is correct. The final sentence says verbatim, 'Neither development generalises the other; they meet exactly at $\\mathbb{R}$.' The exclusivity is false: under the usual embedding of $\\mathbb Q$ into $\\mathbb R$, rational absolute difference is a real-valued metric and positive rational thresholds give the same Cauchy and convergence predicates. This is a false public scope claim, not a proof compression, and licenses removing 'exactly' while making no new exclusivity claim."}
research/audit/wave7-judge-adjudications.jsonl-15-{"id":"lem-finite-minima-of-continuous-unit-interval-maps","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"26dc3faa9cedd7e32c65b31fe82ce940d45d7db159e00ece5c03ea5b635aa74f","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"2c239396af86d1052da0bee9d39f19dfe6fdb5151a4dcbda9cd4926ba09768a8","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T19:32:01Z","note":"F1 cites the product theorem, whose Statement says verbatim, 'The projections are continuous', and def-product-topology says verbatim that finite intersections of projection preimages form a basis. Those clauses make each coordinate inequality set open; step 1.1's citation label is locally incomplete but the declared sources license the claim. The lookup is under thirty seconds, so R1 forbids an edit."}
research/audit/wave7-judge-adjudications.jsonl-16-{"id":"ex-rational-function-field-order","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"d4c9958f6e312f0813641e9ff2f30e8e5bf20ddbbbb18e5a28964b39ff6d62fb","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"9cdd2dabbcf8367cedd558f4fd65d2f6f98bf138c6791387583408e50625683c","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T19:32:01Z","note":"The refuter overlooks its supplied dependency text. cex-ordered-field-not-archimedean proves verbatim, 'Thus $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ eventually have the signs of $a_m$ and $b_n$, respectively'. The finite-root phrase is unused, and the leading-coefficient product rule follows from multiplying the two leading terms in one line. The residual citation compression is nonfatal under thirty seconds; R1 licenses no repair."}
